combinario - merge two words and let AI create a new concept.

This project is pretty much done, I just wanted to mess around with locally hosted LLMs at the time.

This is an attempt of making an open source implementation of Infinite Craft by Neal Agarwal at:
    https://neal.fun/infinite-craft/
Play the original, it's much better than this.

Run via Docker:
    docker compose up
    OR
    make docker-up

Memory constraints:
Since the model is hosted locally, in order to run everything smoothly, your machine would have to have at least 16GB RAM.
You can try to run it with smaller models or better quantized versions, but expect, that output quality will also drop.

LLM notes:
    The recommended model for local generation is Meta Llama 3.1 8B Instruct Q6_K.
    (Q4 K M quant also yields decent results and is a bit lighter in terms of memory usage).
    Models can be downloaded from Hugging Face or any other provider of choice.
    If you want to use another server instead of llama.cpp (e.g. ollama), edit docker compose
    Any server is fine as long as it has OpenAI Chat completions API support.
    VLLM is not recommended - as of now, as it has rocky support for .gguf quants and Apple Silicon (if you are on Mac), but the choice shall rather be made depending on hardware limitations.
